Thought: the ranking varies across windows and the top models are highly correlated, so a per-horizon best-model weighting may capture complementary strengths without fitting noisy global weights.
Action: weights_best_per_horizon
Action Input: {"pool": "pool_full", "metric": "rmse"}

Thought: the leader is the simple median over all models and the margin to the runner-up is indistinguishable, but the series is trend-dominated with moderate ranking stability and correlated errors, so a shrunk inverse-error weighting on the full pool may extract signal without overfitting the three validation windows.
Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"weights": "w2", "rationale": "inverse error weighting with shrinkage 0.5 on full pool to exploit error differences while limiting variance from only 3 validation windows"}

